handoff.notes:
## State

Run 2 (build, sonnet): following the plan below; editing crates/server/tests/api/practice.rs only (play_unless + wrapper, honest_win, new test). Not yet verified.

## Log
(earlier lines of the log were cut here)
lable_parallelism().map_or(1, |cores| cores.get());
           for batch in seeds.chunks(cores) {
               // The place in this batch of the lowest seed that has won so far.
               let lowest_win = AtomicUsize::new(usize::MAX);
               let played: Vec<_> = std::thread::scope(|scope| {
                   let games: Vec<_> = batch
                       .iter()
                       .enumerate()
                       .map(|(place, seed)| {
                           let (setup, lowest_win) = (&setup, &lowest_win);
                           scope.spawn(move || {
                               let beaten = || lowest_win.load(Ordering::Relaxed) < place;
                               let game = play_unless(seed, setup, Human::Ai, &beaten);
                               if matches!(game, Some((_, ClaimedResult::Win, _))) {
                                   lowest_win.fetch_min(place, Ordering::Relaxed);
                               }
                               game
                           })
                       })
                       .collect();
                   games
                       .into_iter()
                       .map(|game| {
                           game.join()
                               .unwrap_or_else(|panic| std::panic::resume_unwind(panic))
                       })
                       .collect()
               });
               let won = batch.iter().zip(played).find_map(|(seed, game)| match game {
                   Some((log, ClaimedResult::Win, state)) => Some((seed, log, state)),
                   _ => None,
               });
               if let Some((seed, log, state)) = won {
                   return (seed.clone(), setup, log, state);
               }
           }
           panic!("the human wins none of {WIN_SEEDS} Easy games");
       })
   }
   ```
   Why the pick is unchanged:
   - A game is abandoned only when `lowest_win < place`, that is, when a lower seed has already won.
   - Any game at or below the final lowest winner never satisfies that, so it always runs to its end.
   - `find_map` over `batch.iter().zip(played)` returns the lowest place, which is what the old `find` returned.
   - If clippy's `type_complexity` fires on `Option<(Vec<Action>, ClaimedResult, GameState)>`, add `type Played = (Vec<Action>, ClaimedResult, GameState);` and use `Option<Played>`. Do not add an `#[allow]`.
4. Add a plain sync test right after `an_honest_win_pays_practice_rates` (see Tests). Name it so that it does not start with `r`, because names starting with `r` land in the other CI group.
5. Do not edit `scripts/ci-shards.toml`.

## Tests

In `crates/server/tests/api/practice.rs`:

```rust
#[test]
fn a_game_the_search_gives_up_on_stops_before_its_next_action() {
    jackioh_cards::register_all();
    let setup = setup(Difficulty::Easy, Vec::new());
    let asked = std::cell::Cell::new(0);
    let abandoned = || {
        asked.set(asked.get() + 1);
        asked.get() > 3
    };
    assert!(play_unless("practice-abandoned", &setup, Human::Ai, &abandoned).is_none());
    assert_eq!(asked.get(), 4, "asked before each action, and not again once it said yes");
}
```

- This asserts that `play_unless` returns `None` when told to stop, and that it asks exactly once before each action.
- It would fail on today's code, which has no `play_unless`.
- The existing six `honest_win` users and the `play(...)` tests keep proving the unchanged path.
- `play` still returns a finished game, because the wrapper's closure never abandons.

Commands, in order. The first build is cold and takes about 4 minutes:
- `cargo fmt --check`
- `cargo clippy -p jackioh-server --all-targets -- -D warnings`
- `time cargo test -p jackioh-server --test server -- api::practice::r`. Before: 27 passed, "finished in 154 s". After: all pass and the test run is **well under 30 s**; I expect about 5–10 s.
- `time cargo test -p jackioh-server --test server -- api::practice:: --skip api::practice::r`. All pass, also fast.
- `cargo test -p jackioh-server --test server -- a_game_the_search_gives_up_on`
- `cargo jackioh spec check`

## Done when

- [ ] `honest_win` and `play_unless` are changed as above, and `play`'s ~40 call sites are untouched.
- [ ] The new test passes.
- [ ] `api::practice::r` (27 tests) passes with a test run well under 30 s, and the other `api::practice::` tests pass. Quote the two `finished in` lines in the report.
- [ ] `cargo fmt --check`, the server clippy line, `cargo jackioh spec check`, and the harness checks (clippy workspace, cargo tests) are green.
- [ ] `scripts/ci-shards.toml` is unchanged, and nothing under `.github/`, `bot/`, `.harness/` or `.squishy/` is touched.
- [ ] The PR text says why no count was raised: the cost was one game that nothing selects, so a count only repeats it per shard, and `bot/tests/test_ci_matrix.py` pins the committed counts.
- [ ] If the practice-rulings run is still above 30 s, report it with the output. Do not paper over it with a count, an `#[ignore]`, or a raised timeout.

## Risks

- **Headroom is thin.**
  - Locally the test step was about 154 s of the job's 7m 1s, so the rest is about 4m 26s: checkout, toolchain, cache restore and an opt-level 2 compile of the engine, cards and server test binary.
  - After the fix I expect about 4m 30s to 4m 40s. That is under 5 minutes, but only by tens of seconds, and I cannot measure CI's runner from here.
  - A count cannot cut that fixed part, because every shard recompiles.
  - If the next run's `ci duration` report still lists the job, see Open questions.
- **Determinism:** the selected game is unchanged (lowest winning seed), and the batch size still follows `available_parallelism` as before. `Ordering::Relaxed` is enough, because `fetch_min` only ever lowers the value and a stale read only stops a game later.
- **Panics in a game thread** still propagate through `join` and `resume_unwind`, as before.
- **Purity:** `crates/server` is not one of the pure crates, and no `crates/engine`, `crates/cards` or `crates/ai` file changes.
- **Pool probe** (`scripts/pool-probe.sh`): behaviour with rotated pools is unchanged, since the same seeds are searched in the same order.

## Open questions

- **Optional, for a person, only if the job is still near 5 minutes after this lands.** The practice groups compile the engine and cards at opt-level 2, while `server` and `server api` build them at opt-level 1. The file's own note says opt-level 2 costs 14 s more compile and runs no faster. I did not measure it for these two groups.
  - It would be an edit in `.github/ci/rust-test.toml`: append `--config profile.test.package.jackioh-engine.opt-level=1 --config profile.test.package.jackioh-cards.opt-level=1` before ` -- ` in the `test` of `server practice` and of `server practice rulings`.
  - The comment above those groups ("each claim has the server re-run a whole practice game's AI") is stale, since the claim no longer runs the AI. A person could refresh it in the same edit.
- **Latent trap, for a person:** a night-bot pull request that changes only `scripts/ci-shards.toml` skips `bot selftest`, yet `bot/tests/test_ci_matrix.py` pins the committed counts. Any future count change needs a person to update that test's `JOBS` list and its `{(shard, shards)} == {(1, 1)}` assertion.
